      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-23_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>Examiner, Saturday, November 23, 1907</head>
        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, November 23, 1907</p>
        <p>WOMAN'S REALM.</p>
        <p>DRESS-FASHION-HOME.</p>
        <p>THE ENGLISH COMPLEXION.</p>
        <p>What shall. we do to save Our complexions? The strawberry-and-cream skin of the English- -woman is threatened. It has been her peculiar characteristic, her proud possession, and it has already shewn signs of waning; and if we lose it—one speaks from a national and not from an individual point of view—it will never be re- gained. Our roses and lilies result from the care of generations of Enzlishwornen. They have washed in morning dew, gone early to bed, avoided the glare of the €.llll, and risked nothing that might endanger the smoothness and clear- ness of their skins. Old books are full of recipes for washes for the complexion which wise mothers of other days taught- their girls from in- fancy to value. Shall we cast away our inheri- tance? What will it avail us if we gain coffers of cigarettes and lose our complexions? But to this favour must we come unless we are more careful to preserve our charm. We eat unwisely, we over-exercise, we _ expose our delicate skins to clouds of dust and merciless winds, we smoke, keep late hours, and do much else that would hove horrified our grandmothers, and—horribile dr we are growing sallow. The thought is horrible, but will we be warned in time?—AMBP.OSIA in the World.</p>
        <p>rutiticF:.o.ly</p>
        <p>ICt 11-</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-23_WidnesExaminer_art0032" n="art0032">
        <head>PRACTICAL COAT FOIL COLD WEATHER.</head>
        <p>PRACTICAL COAT FOIL COLD WEATHER.</p>
        <p>Very cosy and warm is the modish coat which forms the7lubject of our sketch—just the thing for driving, motoring, travelling, or, in cold weather, for theatre wear, or even walking. The original was carried out in a heavy faced cloth of a beautiful shade of chestnut-brown, but the same idea might be very successfully realised in pale grey, biscuit. . dark green. dark blue, or black. From the neck turn back a deep collar and big rounded revers of fur, the collar being</p>
