      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-23_WidnesExaminer_art0096" n="art0096">
        <head>Infhliza Began It.</head>
        <p>Infhliza Began It.</p>
        <p>Brathord Lady's "rielasicholy Story.</p>
        <p>tier Turned into Happiness by</p>
        <p>Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>The case of Mrs. Lily Middows, of Thornton-street, Bradford, is one wh:clishows how seriously Influenza enfeebles the system. Severe depression accompanied her physical weakness, and when melancholy settled upon her its influence upon mind and body was most distressing and life became almost unbearable. Mrs Middows frankly describes her sufferings, and gladly goes on to tell how she was cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Palo People, the remedy that has cured thousands of patients when other medicines have failed.</p>
        <p>IN MELANCHOLY MOOD ALL DAY</p>
        <p>"My illness began with influenza," she told a reporter, "and at one time, I used to sit in a melancholy mood all day, brooding over my bad health. The thought of the many remedies I had vainly tried filled me with an indescribable dread of the future. I became listless, and suffered from severe headaches. At night I was very restlets From nervous slumber I would be awakened by startling dreams. My body was suffused in perspira- tion. Every morning 1 felt so depressed that I could scarcely face the trouble of rising and dressing</p>
        <p>MRS. _ .LY MIDDOWS, Cured of Influenza's After-Effects by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>Food produced nausea, gnawing pains across my chest and shoulders, and violent sickness. My body felt chilled. From a hacking cough I sometimes thought my chest would lyirst. I suffere 1 fro.n an unnatural thirst; my face,-lips, and tongue were discoloured ; the least noise unnerved me and ,et up distressing palpitation."</p>
        <p>TIIE THRILL OF HEALTH RENEWED.</p>
        <p>"I took all kinds of medicines in vain," Mrs Middows added, "but I had never an honr's freedom from pain until I took Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People After a few weeks' treatment with this wonderful blo 4-building tonic medicine, my face, which had been livid, became a more natural colour. As I took Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People I ..could feel a thrill of health through my nerves and rich, warm blood in my veins. My strength grew, my palate cleared, I enjoyed every meal, all pain left' me, arid I became quite cured. I am now in splendid health." Dr. Williams' Pink Pills have become famous because they cure by filling the body with pure, new blood and strengthen the nervous system. Thus they cure 'the A ftpr-Effects of Influenza, 2hills, Chest Complaints, Rilepnatism, Sciatica, Gout, Eczema, and other skin troubles, Anmnia, Indigestion, and Palpita- tions ; also the ailments of women. But only the aenuine pills cure (substitutes. are worse than .useless) and the genuine pills can be obtained from all dealers or direct from the Dr. Williams' Medicine Co., 46, Holborn Viaduct, London, post free, 2s. 9d. for one box, or 13s. 9d. for six boxes. A pamphlet'of parti- cular interest, containing the amount of many cures will be sent post free to all applicants. -</p>
