      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-23_WidnesExaminer_art0103" n="art0103">
        <head>Rochdale Nor!lets at Warrington.</head>
        <p>Rochdale Nor!lets at Warrington.</p>
        <p>The Hornets of Rochdale paid their return visit to the Warrington ground on Saturday, and had to submit to a second detAt at th,r hands of the cup-holders. There %ere 4000 spect,tOrs of a keen but scrambling game. Warring.ton had to make last-minute changes, Cartwright and Jordan replacing Isherwood and Kenyon, while the Hornets were at full strength. Teams and officials : _ _</p>
        <p>-.7 Warrington—Tilley, back; Cartwright, Taylor, Dickenson, and Jordan, three-quarter backs ; Lees (Capt.) and Brooks, half backs ; Thomas, bin! :tars, P. Boardman, A. E. Boardman, Belton, and I:fanner, forwards.</p>
        <p>, Rochdale- Hornets—Tiollinrake, back ; Gibson, Threl- fall, Farrar, and Hartley, three-quarter backs; Baiter and Schofield, half backs ; Dearden. Turner, Crabtree, Richardson, Dutton, and Cockle, forwards. Referee, Mr. H. Farrar, Halifax touch judges, Messrs. Tillotson, Swinton and_Cross, St. 'Helens. After the start the visitors at once assumed the aggressive, and Baxter an.l Sahofield were almost over twice in quick succession. Eventually Baxter served Schofield, and the visitors scored, Farrar improving We points. Rochdale continued to be the aggressors, until Schofield was hurt, and directly this t layer had retired, Warrington played a strong forward game, and Lees, Brooks and Jordan all made futile efforts to cross. Thomas wiped off two points of the deficit, with a ppnalty shot, and then Shugars crossed near the posts. but Thomas failed at goal, the score at half-time being 5 points each. Turning round, the visitors resumed without Schofield. Warrington immediately attacked, and after Jordan had tried to rush through, a rapid movement between Brooks and Dickenson led op to a try to the three-quarter, Thomas just missing the goal. Rochdale rallied, and flihson made a great effort on the right, but Cartwright accounted for him. Near the close Warrington again pressed, as the result of brilliant forward play, and Belton crossed. Result :—Warrington, 1 goal 3 tries (II points), Rochdale Hornets 1 goal 1 try (5 points).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-11-23_WidnesExaminer_art0104" n="art0104">
        <head>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION. NI,'ARIZINGTON "A" v. ROCHDALE "A".</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION. NI,'ARIZINGTON "A" v. ROCHDALE "A".</p>
        <p>This match was played at Rochdale on Saturday, and though Warrington had a weakened team they managed to win in substantial style.ln the first half Forster made a fine run and scored under the posts,also adding a goal. Good combination by dui b.Acks resulted in further tries to Tinklor and Landor, Preston kicking.another goal. Half time : Warrington 2 goals 3 tries (13 points) Rochdale nil. In the secnnd half the game was more evenly cont,r,ted and both sides scored five points. Morley got the try for Warrington and Preston goaled. Final : Warrington 3 goals, 4 tries (13 points): Roch- dale 5 points. During the progress of the game a blacksmith named Fred Farrar, aged 23 years, who was Watching the game on tbe main line overlooking the ground. was knocked down by a passing train and expired before his arrival at the Infirmary. . Oldham</p>
        <p>P. 6 Wigan</p>
