        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. lINICIPAL BY F-ELECTION 1907.—T0 THE ELECTORS OF LATCHFORD WARD. LADIES AND GENTL • MEN, I have been requested by many Friends and also by the liberal Ward Committee to become a candidate to fill the vacancy caused by the elevation of my Friend, Mr. Luke Elli,on to the Aldermanic Bench, and have consented to do so. I come from a very old Warrington family and have lived in the Ward for 25 years. I am a small Property Owner in the Ward and have taken taken the greatest interest as Secretary and President of the Liberal Ward Committee for over 20 years. I know the many recpairements of the Ward—Victoria Bridge, the Est nsion of Victoria Park, the New Bridge at Howley, and many °the's. These improvements I consider of the first importance,and would do my best to bring them about. 1 take the greatest interest •in Friendly Societies, and would do all In my power to defend and protect 4arae. I have served for tbree years on the vdn cation Committee as the first representative of the United Friendly Si,eieties of the town, being chosen by a Meeting of Representatives of all the Societies at the Town Hall. I was a member of the School Attendance anl Finance • Sub-Committees, and my attendance during the three years was near the highest of 36 members forming the Council, and am at present a manager for two Schools in the Ward—St. James' and Grappenhall-road Council Schools. As a Churchman I have the highest possible regard for the people who have built the Schools and educated our Children in the past, am! I would net support any serious interferenfse with the present method. lam not aware that the Warrington Education Committee have attempted to prevent any Parent having his Children educated in the same faith as himself, and if any attempt was made to do so I sbould oppose it. I consider the work that has been done by the Education Committee is splendid, and has been accomplished with little or no friction, which ii a great thing when you come to consider that many shades of Religion and Politica are represented. With regard to other Corporation undertakings, I should support what I consider to be in the best interests of the town generally. If electcd I shall do my best to serve you and my native town faithfully and well. Soliciting the favour of your votes and support, I beg to remain, Ladies and Gentlemen, Yours respectfully, WILLIAM BIBBY, 13, Arpley Etreet, Warrington.</p>
